v1.1 Update

This update adds a new layer of strategy to Coaster Capital by introducing rare Legend Gold Cards and more detailed festival/event requirements.

The biggest new feature is the addition of Legend Gold Cards, which are special ultra-rare cards that can change the direction of a season. Only two Legend cards exist in the deck, making them much rarer than normal attractions and turning their auction appearances into major bidding moments.

The first Legend card is Golden Comet, 1928, a legendary wooden coaster built around massive nostalgia and long-term legacy value. Its special ability gives the owning park bonus legacy at the end of each season, making it valuable even beyond its featured-event score.

The second Legend card is The Lost Mill, a legendary dark ride with a special bonus ability. It counts as both a Dark Ride and a Historic card for bonuses, allowing it to fit into more scoring combinations and making it especially powerful during heritage-focused events.

Legend cards also received a distinct gold visual style so they stand out from normal attraction cards. They are designed to feel like rare auction moments rather than just another card in the lineup.

The festival/event system was also expanded. Events now show more than just the basic scoring focus. Each festival card now includes:

Scoring focus
Shows which stats matter most for that event, such as Thrill, Nostalgia, Capacity, Theme, or Food.

Type bonuses
Shows which attraction types receive extra points, such as Coaster, Water, Food, Dark Ride, Family, or Upgrade.

Type penalties
Shows if certain attraction types lose value during an event, such as outdoor rides being weaker during rainy weather.

Park support
Explains how your whole park can still help the season through food stands, capacity, and upgrades, even if those cards are not the featured attraction.

This makes festivals easier to understand and gives players more meaningful choices. Instead of simply picking the card with the biggest matching number, players now have to think about card type, event bonuses, whole-park support, maintenance, and rare Legend abilities.

Overall, the update makes Coaster Capital more exciting, more strategic, and more rewarding by adding rare chase cards and clearer event requirements.
